  "erasure_decision": "At target1 after eight successful meals, the hypothetical organism has E56, pc0, feedback1, feedback-register1 and nursery24. Counterfactually erasing only its port register adds five failed-path dispatches before reacquisition. Under zero or one identical scalar handling fee, cap spill falls by the same five and both arms give parent27+child12 at first birth. Thus this first-birth construction shows a conditional timing saving, not retained-energy or offspring-count advantage. No erasure operation or intervention protocol was executed/admitted; the handling fee is an illustrative equal-cost scalar, not a changed law. With handling1, successful FORAGE is at global60, before the initial-packet target flip at64; only DIVIDE reaches64. Input/release occurs at64 and requires accounting in any whole-world comparison. The earlier incorrect wording that packet8 retained seed-parity target at64 was rejected independently and preserved locally; no numerical row depended on that wording.",
  "retired_subproblem": "Do not keep extending the unified six-role site3 entry as if three spare slots guaranteed a lifecycle. The different stationary success-gated witness uses no navigation/SENSE and remains subject to natural-origin and fair-competition proof.",
